#
# holt — Dockerfile for a ctags that does not have it.
#
# Loaded ONLY after holt has MEASURED that this toolchain cannot extract Dockerfile symbols, and
# defined under a PRIVATE name. Both matter, and the reason is not hypothetical: this definition
# used to live in the always-loaded pack under the real name `Dockerfile`, and the moment upstream
# ctags gained its own Dockerfile parser the load became FATAL — "Language \"Dockerfile\" already
# defined", ctags exits, and holt gets ZERO symbols from EVERY file in the repository. Silence,
# which reads as "these agents share nothing".
#
# A private name cannot collide with a builtin. The measurement gate means a real builtin parser
# is never replaced by these regexes when one exists.
#
### Dockerfile #################################################################
--langdef=HoltDockerfile
--map-HoltDockerfile=+(Dockerfile)
--map-HoltDockerfile=+(Dockerfile.*)
--map-HoltDockerfile=+(*.Dockerfile)
--map-HoltDockerfile=+.dockerfile
--kinddef-HoltDockerfile=s,stage,build stages
--kinddef-HoltDockerfile=a,arg,build arguments
--regex-HoltDockerfile=/^[ \t]*[Ff][Rr][Oo][Mm][ \t]+[^ \t]+[ \t]+[Aa][Ss][ \t]+([a-zA-Z0-9_.-]+)/\1/s/
--regex-HoltDockerfile=/^[ \t]*[Aa][Rr][Gg][ \t]+([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)/\1/a/
